    {
      "page_title": "Generated Methods & Decorator Params",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What Is Generated",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Three methods by default: `__init__`, `__repr__`, `__eq__`",
            "`__init__` takes one argument per ==field==",
            "`__repr__` prints `Point(x=1, y=2)`",
            "`__eq__` compares fields as **tuples**"
          ],
          "style": "star",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "@dataclass(init=True,",
            "    repr=True, eq=True,",
            "    order=False,",
            "    unsafe_hash=False,",
            "    frozen=False)"
          ],
          "note": "the classic six parameters"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Newer param",
            "Default",
            "Since"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "match_args",
              "True",
              "3.10"
            ],
            [
              "kw_only",
              "False",
              "3.10"
            ],
            [
              "slots",
              "False",
              "3.10"
            ],
            [
              "weakref_slot",
              "False",
              "3.11"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. How It Behaves",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`__eq__` runs only if `other.__class__ is self.__class__`",
            "Otherwise it returns ==NotImplemented==",
            "Fields are compared as tuples: `(x, y) == (x, y)`"
          ],
          "style": "number",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "eq",
            "frozen",
            "__hash__"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "False",
              "any",
              "inherited object hash"
            ],
            [
              "True",
              "True",
              "generated from fields"
            ],
            [
              "True",
              "False",
              "set to **None**"
            ],
            [
              "unsafe_hash=True",
              "any",
              "generated, even if mutable"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "You write",
            "@dataclass does"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "own `__init__`",
              "keeps yours"
            ],
            [
              "`__repr__` in body",
              "keeps yours"
            ],
            [
              "repr=False",
              "no `__repr__` made"
            ],
            [
              "order=True + own `__lt__`",
              "**TypeError**"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "unsafe_hash",
          "text": "Mutating a key after insert breaks dict/set lookups."
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "p = Point(1, 2)",
            "p == Point(1, 2)  # True",
            "p == (1, 2)       # False",
            "{p: 1}  # TypeError: unhashable"
          ],
          "note": "eq alone kills hashing"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Example : `Point(1, 2) == Point(1, 2)` is True, but `Point(1, 2) == (1, 2)` is ==False==.",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "pink"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Common Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Assuming equality ignores class: `Point(1,2) == (1,2)` is **False**",
            "Using an instance as a dict key without `frozen=True` or `unsafe_hash`",
            "Setting order=True while hand-writing `__lt__`"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Tip",
          "text": "Need set members or dict keys? Use ==frozen=True== instead of unsafe_hash."
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`match_args=True` creates `__match_args__`",
            "It lists field names in definition order",
            "Keyword patterns work even without it",
            "Pattern positions follow the **field order**"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "python",
      "subtitle": "What @dataclass writes"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Pattern Matching and Hashability",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Worked Example",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "@dataclass",
            "class Point:",
            "    x: int",
            "    y: int",
            "match Point(1, 2):",
            "    case Point(x, y): ..."
          ],
          "note": "positional needs match_args=True"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Making It Hashable",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "@dataclass(frozen=True)",
            "class Point:",
            "    x: int",
            "    y: int",
            "",
            "seen = {Point(1, 2): 'a'}"
          ],
          "note": "eq + frozen generates __hash__"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Frozen + eq: hash built from the fields",
            "Equal instances give equal hashes",
            "Mutable + eq: hash is **None**, so unhashable"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Reading __match_args__",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "Point.__match_args__  # ('x', 'y')",
            "",
            "match Point(0, 5):",
            "    case Point(x=0, y=y): ..."
          ],
          "note": "keyword patterns skip match_args"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`match_args=False` removes positional patterns",
            "Keyword patterns like `Point(x=0)` still work",
            "`kw_only` fields are left out of `__match_args__`"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Pattern",
            "Needs match_args?"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`Point(x, y)`",
              "**yes**"
            ],
            [
              "`Point(x=0, y=y)`",
              "no"
            ],
            [
              "`Point()`",
              "no, type check only"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Tip",
          "text": "Hash a mutable dataclass with ==unsafe_hash== only if you never change its fields."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Remember",
          "text": "Three methods by default. Hash depends on the eq and frozen pair."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "python",
      "subtitle": "What @dataclass writes"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "field(): Defaults and Options",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Simple Defaults",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Simple default: `x: int = 0`",
            "A non-default field after a default field raises **TypeError**",
            "`ClassVar[...]` keeps an attribute out of the fields entirely"
          ],
          "style": "star",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "@dataclass",
            "class C:",
            "    a: int = 0",
            "    b: int       # TypeError",
            "    n: ClassVar[int] = 5  # no field"
          ],
          "note": "defaults must come last"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Mutable Defaults",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`items: list = []` raises **ValueError**",
            "A shared list, dict or set would leak across instances",
            "The check rejects ==unhashable== defaults (list, dict, set)",
            "A hashable mutable object slips through: rule is by hash (3.11)"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "from dataclasses import field",
            "",
            "items: list[int] = field(",
            "    default_factory=list)"
          ],
          "note": "factory runs fresh per instance"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "default_factory",
            "Gives each instance"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`dict`, `set`",
              "empty container"
            ],
            [
              "`lambda: [1, 2]`",
              "new [1, 2]"
            ],
            [
              "`uuid.uuid4`",
              "fresh UUID"
            ],
            [
              "`datetime.now`",
              "creation time"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Any ==zero-argument callable== works as a factory.",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. field() Options",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Option",
            "Effect"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`init=False`",
              "out of __init__; set in __post_init__"
            ],
            [
              "`repr=False`",
              "hidden from __repr__ (secrets)"
            ],
            [
              "`compare=False`",
              "out of __eq__ and ordering"
            ],
            [
              "`hash=None`",
              "follows compare"
            ],
            [
              "`kw_only=True`",
              "one field keyword-only (3.10)"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "@dataclass",
            "class User:",
            "    name: str",
            "    pw: str = field(repr=False)",
            "    uid: int = field(init=False,",
            "                     default=0)"
          ],
          "note": "repr hides pw, init skips uid"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "w: float = field(metadata={",
            "    \"unit\": \"kg\"})",
            "fields(C)[0].metadata[\"unit\"]"
          ],
          "note": "dataclasses itself ignores metadata"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "metadata",
          "text": "Read-only mappingproxy, there for libraries to read."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Common Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`x: int = field()` still counts as **required**",
            "`default` plus `default_factory` raises **ValueError**",
            "Writing `= []` instead of `default_factory=list`",
            "Annotating a constant without `ClassVar` makes it a field"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "python",
      "subtitle": "Defaults and Options"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "frozen, slots and Ordering",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What frozen Gives",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`frozen=True` writes `__setattr__` and `__delattr__` that raise **FrozenInstanceError**",
            "Only ==pseudo-immutable==: bindings fixed, a list field still mutates",
            "frozen + `eq=True` generates `__hash__`: dict keys, set members",
            "Generated `__init__` uses `object.__setattr__`: slightly slower per instance"
          ],
          "style": "star",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "@dataclass(frozen=True)",
            "class P:",
            "    xs: list",
            "p = P([1])",
            "p.xs.append(2)  # allowed",
            "p.xs = []  # FrozenInstanceError"
          ],
          "note": "shallow: contents still mutate"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. slots=True (3.10)",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Builds a **new class** with `__slots__`: no `__dict__`",
            "Wins: lower memory, slightly faster attribute access",
            "Undeclared attribute assignment raises `AttributeError`",
            "Defaults stay in `__init__`; class dict handling is rewritten",
            "Hand-written `__slots__` clashes with class-level defaults"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "@dataclass(slots=True)",
            "class V:",
            "    n: int = 0",
            "v = V()",
            "v.z = 1  # AttributeError"
          ],
          "note": "no __dict__, no stray attributes"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Different class object",
          "text": "The decorator returns a new class. Zero-argument `super()` in methods breaks before 3.14."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. order=True Sorting",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Adds `__lt__`, `__le__`, `__gt__`, `__ge__` comparing fields as ==tuples==",
            "Fields compared in **definition order**",
            "Needs `eq=True`, else ValueError; same class only",
            "`field(compare=False)` drops a field from ordering",
            "Reorder fields to change sort priority"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "@dataclass(order=True)",
            "class Version:",
            "    major: int",
            "    minor: int",
            "    patch: int",
            "sorted(versions)  # major first"
          ],
          "note": "field order is the sort key"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Flag",
            "Generates",
            "Needs"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "frozen=True",
              "__setattr__, __delattr__, __hash__",
              "eq=True for hash"
            ],
            [
