          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. How fields are collected",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Base fields are gathered in ==reverse MRO== order, then the subclass's own",
            "Redefining a base field keeps its **original position**, with the new type and default",
            "A non-dataclass base adds __no fields__; only `@dataclass` classes are scanned",
            "The subclass needs its own `@dataclass`, or new fields never reach `__init__`"
          ],
          "style": "star",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "@dataclass",
            "class Base:",
            "    a: int = 1",
            "    b: int = 2",
            "@dataclass",
            "class Sub(Base):",
            "    a: str = 'x'  # still first"
          ],
          "note": "Order: a, b. Type of a is str"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Example : `Sub()` builds `Sub(a='x', b=2)`; field `a` keeps slot one but takes the ==new default==.",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "pink"
        },
